   • 3 live server(s), none runs a removed plugin's hook ✔
   🌙 2 socket(s) did not answer — a socket outlives its server, so
      these are most likely corpses, and a corpse runs no timer
      read why: coredumpctl list tmux   (a server that crashed leaves its core there)
   🌙 1 live server(s) did not name their build — not graded against the pin
   🌙 1 live server(s) still run a build older than the pin
      ⇒ each keeps the binary it started on until it ends; a new server takes the pin
      ⇒ no apply restarts them, and no seat inside one should: a restart ends EVERY
        session on that server — while crews share one server, that is every crew
        on it, the reader's own session among them
      next: a human decides when those sessions may end. once each crew holds its
        own server (nheuron#44), a crew's restart moves only that crew to the pin
      servers: prior=3.2a
   ✋ ConstraintError: 1 live server(s) hold a default-terminal the conf does NOT declare
      ⇒ each pane spawned there inherits that TERM and EMITS to match, so
        an 8-colour entry clamps colour at its source — invisible to every
        claim above, which read the conf rather than the server
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 2.8.tmux --mode apply
      ⚠️ a pane that ALREADY exists keeps its spawn-time TERM, so open a
        new window or pane to see the repair
      servers: prior=screen
   ✋ ConstraintError: 2 of 4 live pane(s) hold a TERM the conf does NOT declare
      ⇒ TERM is copied into a pane's child AT SPAWN and never re-read, so
        these predate the conf reaching their server. the app inside each
        reads that TERM, concludes 8 colours, and EMITS only 8-colour
        codes — a clamp at the SOURCE that no client feature can undo
      ⇒ no re-apply repairs a pane. the server is already correct, so a
        NEW pane or window spawns right; these carry their old copy until
        they exit
      fix, per affected pane — whichever reaches it:
        • a pane you sit at:  open a new one (prefix c / prefix %)
        • a grove's duct:     rhx duct.reboot --on 'duct://<grove>/<tree>/<role>'
          ⇒ the session, its name, its scrollback, and its cwd survive;
            only the pane's child dies, and its replacement spawns with
            the TERM the server now declares
   • the conf declares no terminal-features — no client claim to grade
